# Configuration for the Cirro Data Transfer Utility. Copy to .env and adjust;
# uvicorn loads it with --env-file. See the README "Credentials" section:
# Cirro upload auth is an in-app login and must NOT go here, and sources
# normally use ambient SDK credentials (gcloud ADC, ~/.aws) rather than this
# file. Short-lived source credentials below are a dev exception.

# Cirro tenant host (host only, no scheme).
CIRRO_BASE_URL=app.cirro.bio

# Where the SQLite DB and the staging/scratch tempdirs live.
# CIRRO_TRANSFER_HOME=~/.cirro-transfer

# Datasets transferred concurrently.
CIRRO_TRANSFER_CONCURRENCY=1

# How the UI receives live progress. "auto" tries the SSE stream and falls back
# to polling if it doesn't come through; "poll" skips the attempt, for a proxy
# known to buffer or drop streaming responses; "sse" disables the fallback.
# CIRRO_TRANSFER_EVENTS_TRANSPORT=auto

# ---- s3:// source credentials (boto3 reads these from the environment) ----
# Values are literal — no quotes, no `export`, no interpolation. The worker
# reads them once at server start, so restart uvicorn after refreshing them.
# Prefer a named profile (credentials stay in ~/.aws, refreshed by the CLI):
# AWS_PROFILE=my-profile
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2
#
# Or paste temporary STS credentials (all three; omit the token for long-lived
# keys). These expire, so an unexplained AccessDenied means re-issue them:
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=ASIAEXAMPLE0000000000
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=wJalrXUtnFEMIK7MDENGbPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=IQoJb3JpZ2luX2VjEXAMPLETOKEN
